@startuml implementation-issue-states
' cumin works - states of an implementation issue.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: [guard] / effect, with the name of the transition in front.
' Every guard and effect names who acts. Two actions change no state; they are notes.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / the Planner or the Owner writes the issue

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / cumin waits for a free slot

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the Implementer works

state "checking" as Checks
Checks : do / GitHub runs the required checks

state "reviewing" as Reviewing
Reviewing : do / the Reviewer reviews the pull request

state "awaiting-merge-decision" as OwnerReview
OwnerReview : do / the Owner reviews the pull request

state "merging" as Merging
Merging : do / cumin merges the pull request,\nthen closes the issue

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Owner answers

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Ready --> Implementing : request the implementation\n[the Owner added ready, the blockers are closed,\ncumin has a free slot]\n/ cumin requests the implementation\nfrom the Implementer
Implementing --> Checks : wait for the checks\n[no Implementer runs, cumin verified\nthe pull request]\n/ cumin adds the closing link
Implementing --> Implementing : request the implementation again\n[no Implementer runs, cumin could not verify\nthe pull request, first time]\n/ cumin requests the Implementer again
Implementing --> Decision : stop the implementation for the Owner\n[no Implementer runs, and: the Implementer asked\na question, cumin could not verify the pull request\nthe second time, or a conflict resolution left the head commit]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Checks --> Reviewing : request the review\n[the required checks passed]\n/ cumin requests the review from the Reviewer
Checks --> Implementing : request a check fix\n[a required check failed, cumin's fix\nrequests are under the limit]\n/ cumin requests a check fix from the Implementer
Checks --> Decision : stop for failed checks\n[a required check failed, the fix requests\nare at the limit]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Checks --> Implementing : request a conflict resolution\n[the pull request conflicts]\n/ cumin requests a conflict resolution\nfrom the Implementer
Checks --> Decision : stop for missing checks\n[a required check gave no result in time]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Reviewing --> Implementing : request a review fix\n[no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer requested changes\non the head commit, the rounds are under the limit]\n/ cumin requests a review fix from the Implementer
Reviewing --> Merging : start the merge\n[no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer approved the\nhead commit, the checks passed, risk/low]\n/ cumin changes the label
Reviewing --> OwnerReview : ask the Owner to decide the merge\n[no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer approved the\nhead commit, the checks passed,\nrisk/medium or risk/high]\n/ cumin requests the Owner's review\nand notifies the Owner
Reviewing --> Reviewing : request the cause from the Reviewer\n[no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer requested changes,\nthe rounds are at the limit, no explanation yet]\n/ cumin requests the cause from the Reviewer
Reviewing --> Decision : stop at the round limit\n[the Reviewer wrote the explanation of the cause]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Reviewing --> Decision : stop the review for the Owner\n[no Reviewer runs, and: the Reviewer asked a question,\nor the Reviewer left no review the second time]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Reviewing --> Checks : go back to the checks\n[no Reviewer runs, and: the head commit moved,\nor a required check does not pass]\n/ cumin changes the label
Reviewing --> Reviewing : request the review again\n[no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer left no review\non the head commit, first time]\n/ cumin requests the review again
OwnerReview --> Merging : start the merge\n[the Owner approved the head commit,\nthe checks passed]\n/ cumin changes the label
OwnerReview --> Implementing : request a response to the Owner's review\n[the Owner requested changes]\n/ cumin requests a response from the Implementer
OwnerReview --> Implementing : request a conflict resolution\n[the pull request conflicts]\n/ cumin requests a conflict resolution\nfrom the Implementer
OwnerReview --> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Merging --> [*] : close the merged issue\n[GitHub shows the pull request as merged]\n/ cumin closes the issue
Merging --> Checks : go back to the checks\n[the pull request is not merged, the approval\nor the checks no longer hold]\n/ cumin changes the label
Merging --> Implementing : request a conflict resolution\n[GitHub refused the merge: conflict]\n/ cumin requests a conflict resolution\nfrom the Implementer
Merging --> Decision : stop the merge for the Owner\n[GitHub refused the merge for another\nlasting reason]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Decision --> Ready : the Owner adds ready

note "copy the labels to the pull request: in every state, the labels of the issue differ from\nthose of its pull request / cumin copies the labels." as I11
note "write the follow-up note: the issue is closed and its pull request is merged\n/ cumin writes the follow-up note." as I9

legend right
  A box is a state: a label on GitHub, without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
  An arrow is a transition: [guard] / effect, each with its actor. The first line is the name of the transition in issue-states.md.
  Every guard reads only facts on GitHub and "no agent runs for this issue".
endlegend

@enduml
